dental                package:AA                     R Documentation

Data on Dental Status of Children

Description:

     The 'dental' data frame has 9 rows and 2 columns.

     This data set gives the dental status of children according to an
     index that takes values in 0-8, as obtained from a prospective
     survey of school children.

Usage:

     data(dental)

Format:

     The 'dental' data frame contains the following columns:

     'index' the dental status of children according to an index that
          takes values in 0-8;

     'frequency' number of children who have the corresponding detal
          status.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Bohning, D., Dietz, E., Schlattman,P., Mendorca, L. and Kirchner,
     U. (1991).  The zero-inflated Poisson model and the decayed,
     missing and filled teeth index in dental epidemiology.  _Journal
     of the Royal Statistical Society, Series A_, *162*, 195-209.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Problem 29.

     Castillo, J.D. and Lopez-Ratera, A. (2006).  Saddlepoint
     approximation in exponential models with boundary points. 
     _Bernoulli_, *12*, 491-500.

     Deng, D. and Paul, S.R. (2005).  Score tests for zero-inflation
     and over-dispersion in generalized linear models.  _Statistica
     Sinica_, *15*, 257-276.

Examples:

     data(dental)
     barplot(dental$frequency)
